the PRC law, all land in the PRC is owned by the government and cannot be sold to an individual or company. The government grants individuals
and companies the right to use parcels of land for specified periods of time. Land use rights are stated at cost less accumulated amortization.
<ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c0" continuedAt="_ScheduleOfIndefiniteLivedIntangibleAssetsTableTextBlock-c0_cont_1" escape="true" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfIndefiniteLivedIntangibleAssetsTableTextBlock" id="ixv-11269">Land use rights are amortized using the straight-line method with the following estimated useful lives:</ix:nonNumeric></span></p></ix:continuation>

